105:- **Which route to the triangle inequality was taken.** The proof above obtains (N3) by expanding $\lVert x+y\rVert_2^{2}$ and applying Cauchy-Schwarz. The alternative is to quote [[thm-minkowski-finite]] at the rational exponent $p = 2$, which states the same inequality directly; that route is equally legitimate and is the one [[lem-p-norms-are-norms-and-induce-the-published-metrics]] uses for a general exponent. Only one of the two is used here, so no statement is proved twice.

